{
    "background_story": "Garrett, a free-spirited artist, had always been drawn to the exotic and the unknown. During his travels to the South Pacific, he became enchanted with the frangipani flower, with its delicate white petals and sweet fragrance. He was captivated by the way the locals used the flowers to create beautiful leis and adorn their homes. Garrett settled on a small island, where he built a seaside studio surrounded by frangipani trees. He spent his days painting the island's vibrant colors and his nights strumming his guitar under the starry sky, surrounded by the intoxicating scent of the frangipani. As his art gained recognition, Garrett's island home became a haven for fellow artists and travelers seeking inspiration. The frangipani flower became a symbol of his carefree spirit and his ability to find beauty in the simplest things.",
